// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27f/lesson_reel.t27 -- a reel of any lesson of course 0, in English or Russian, on the
// token_floor template: the lesson's title, goal and task spoken in the owner's voice and written
// under it, its spec on the three glass cards, and its page as the call to action.
//
// WHY: the owner asked for a reel for every lesson, in two languages, made by a generator from the
// topic rather than one reel at a time, with the source in t27. A lesson is an index into
// reel_topics; this module turns the index and a language into every text layer and the sound
// graph of the reel, so lesson 1 and lesson 27 come out of the same code.
//
// HOW (main, by LR_MODE; LR_T the lesson 0..26, LR_LANG 0 en / 1 ru):
//   0  phrase LR_K's text, UTF-8, for the voice service: 0 the title, 1 the goal, 2 the task
//   1  text file LR_K of the reel: the tags, the cards' lines, the page, the caption chunks
//   2  how many text files there are
//   3  the two ffmpeg -filter_complex_script graphs, tall then wide, given LR_MS0..LR_MS2, the
//      phrases' lengths in ms as the voice service returned them. Inputs: 0 the frames,
//      1..3 the phrases' wavs, 4 the music.
//   4  the beat graph (t27#10603), given LR_MS0..LR_MS2: inputs 0..2 the open, main and close
//      scene clips, crossfaded on whole frames at the beat clock's cuts and trimmed to the reel
//   5  mode 3's two graphs laid over mode 4's beat video (t27#10609): inputs 0..2 the scene
//      clips, 3..5 the phrases' wavs, 6 the music. The captions, tags, cards and address are shown
//      on whole frames inside the scenes and never on a crossfade (t27#10614, t27#10628,
//      beat_piece_*)
// Every text that comes from the lesson goes through a textfile, so no quote, colon or percent in
// a lesson can break the graph (and drawtext runs with expansion=none).
//
// TIMING: the phrases follow one another from the voice offset with a gap. When they would run
// into the call to action's hold, the voice is sped up (atempo, pitch kept) up to
// TEMPO_MAX_PERMILLE; when the three still do not fit, the task is dropped and the reel speaks the
// title and the goal. A caption chunk is a run of whole words up to CHUNK_CHARS, timed by its
// share of its phrase's letters -- an estimate, not a word-level alignment.
//
// BEATS (t27#10596, R4a of t27#10560): reel_beats.t27 gives every reel three scenes, open, main
// and close; the beat clock below says when each is on screen. Cut 0 is the goal phrase's start
// and cut 1 is where the address takes over, so the picture turns with the sentence rather than at
// fixed thirds of the reel, which on lesson 1 land inside a spoken phrase (the control test). A
// title too short to read holds the open beat to BEAT_OPEN_FLOOR_MS, unless the voice reaches the
// address before BEAT_SPOKEN_MIN_MS: then the open beat gives way and the main beat keeps its
// scene (one point on the test grid, 200/1500/13100 ms, where the task is dropped). Every cut is a crossfade of
// reel.t27's TRANSITION_FRAMES, centred on the cut. The clock lives here, not in a module of its
// own, because a module that imports phrase_start, cta_from or voice_fits from this file gets
// none of them: t27c's splicer finds a second declaration of each in this file's imports and
// drops both (t27#10556).
//
// NOT CLAIMED: the backdrop is token_floor's physics world, not a picture of the lesson; its frame
// labels are the physics reel's. Mode 5 lays the same captions and address over every scene, in
// the same places, and only their windows change with the beat. The cards keep token_floor_mux's
// windows, cut to their scene's frames as the captions are; a card with no room is dropped.
// Both cuts are centred on a sentence change, so a crossfade can begin under the last words
// of a phrase: mode 5 then drops a caption with too little room left (the cost tests). Cut 1 is
// capped at BEAT_CUT1_LAST_MS so mode 5 holds the address for REEL_CTA_MIN_MS (t27#10629): on a
// voice the reel had to speed up, lesson 1's measured voice among them, crossfade 1 then starts
// up to 184 ms before the task's last word ends, in modes 4 and 5 alike. The scenes themselves
// are R3.
// phi^2 + 1/phi^2 = 3 | TRINITY

module lesson_reel;

